// Macro terrain from the engine's own SDF, contact and mesh systems: a sector of a ring of walls (a basin, a caldera, a
// crater's rim) as a few superellipsoid masses with fBm relief over their union. A library: it emits no document; a world
// imports it and places one creation per sector, so each sector is separately editable and bakes as its own group.
//
//   import "../standard/terrain"
//
// A sector is authored in its own frame: author +Z points out from the ring's centre and the creation is placed at that
// centre, turned by the placement's yawDegrees. With the author frame's half turn, a placement yaw of (compass + 180)
// points the sector at compass bearing `compass` (0 is world +Z, 90 is world +X): terrainYaw(compass) says so once.
//
// Contact rides the masses alone. The debug world's analytic provider collides each superellipsoid with its exact Lp
// surface, and creation noise is render-only relief (CreationNoiseDocument), so keep its amplitude to the error a body
// may sink into or float over the drawn slope. Walkable decks on the terrain are separate creations without noise.

// The placement yaw that points a sector authored along author +Z at a compass bearing.
let terrainYaw = 180

// One wall mass: an ellipsoid (exponent 2) or a cliffier superellipsoid sunk below the floor plane, so that the floor
// plane cuts it at `foot` from the ring's centre and it rises to `peak` above that plane.
//   radial      the mass's half-extent along the sector's outward axis
//   across      its half-extent along the ring
//   offset      its centre's shift along the ring (author +X), for ridges that do not repeat
//   sink        the fraction of its vertical half-extent below the floor plane, so a deeper sink steepens the foot
// With exponent 2 the centre stands radial · √(1 − sink²) beyond the foot; a larger exponent moves the foot outward by
// at most a few percent, which the authored foot absorbs.
template terrainMass(label, foot, peak, radial, across, offset = 0, sink = 0.3, exponent = 2, material = 0) {
  // A union only: a creation's smooth blends are bounded at CreationDocument.MaxSmooth (half a metre), far under a
  // wall's scale, and the analytic provider collides any blend as the hard union.
  shape Superellipsoid $"{label}" {
    exponent: exponent
    material: material
    position [offset, (0 - ((peak / (1 - sink)) * sink)), (foot + (radial * squareRoot((1 - (sink * sink)))))]
    scale [across, (peak / (1 - sink)), radial]
  }
}

// The floor plane's cut through a sector: everything composed before it is intersected with the slab from `below` under
// the floor plane up to `top`, so the masses' buried halves neither bake nor size the sector's lattice. A detail shape:
// contact keeps colliding each mass whole, and nothing stands under the floor.
template terrainFloorCut(top, below = 10, reach = 2000) {
  shape Box "floor-cut" {
    blend: Intersection
    detail: true
    material: 0
    position [0, ((top - below) / 2), 0]
    scale [reach, ((top + below) / 2), reach]
  }
}

// The fBm relief over a sector's union: amplitude in metres, frequency in cells per metre. Six octaves of lacunarity 2
// put the finest at 32 times the base frequency.
template terrainRelief(seed, amplitude = 4, frequency = 0.02, octaves = 6) {
  noise {
    frequency: frequency
    amplitude: amplitude
    octaves: octaves
    gain: 0.5
    lacunarity: 2
    seed: seed
  }
}
